      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! I found the answer.\n\nAccording to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by:\n\n1. **Never storing it in the Hub\u0027s process** \u2014 The key is not held in the Hub\u0027s environment variables or process memory.\n\n2. **Using a local secrets loader** \u2014 At startup, a secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file (which exists outside the repository and is not version-controlled).\n\n3. **Injecting into child processes only** \u2014 The key is injected directly into the environment of spawned child processes (Ingest agent and Query agent) immediately before they start, not inherited from the Hub.\n\nThis design ensures that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the Anthropic API credential by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key never exists there in the first place \u2014 it only lives in the short-lived child process that actually needs to call the Anthropic API.",
